    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Maps Fonnte's real inbound webhook payload (Gate 6J-C1 verified capture)\n// to ADOP's canonical envelope shape (task LOCK A).\n//\n// Gate 6J-C1.1: n8n's real Webhook node output is\n// { headers, params, query, body, webhookUrl, executionMode } — Fonnte's\n// fields live under .body, never at the top level. Reading $input.item.json\n// directly (the pre-6J-C1.1 bug) picked up that wrapper instead of the\n// actual payload, so every field below silently resolved to ''. The\n// direct-body fallback (body = input when input.body is missing/non-object)\n// exists ONLY for compatibility/testing — e.g. this workflow's own contract\n// test invoking the node against a bare Fonnte payload with no wrapper. It\n// is a strict typeof check, not `||`, so a wrapper with a missing or\n// non-object .body falls through to an all-empty envelope rather than\n// throwing — Validate Required Fields (the next node) then fails it closed.\n//\n// senderid is a WhatsApp sender identity/LID, never a message id — never\n// used here. inboxid can be 0 or absent, so it is only trusted as a\n// providerMessageId when it is a positive integer; otherwise\n// providerMessageId is left OFF the envelope entirely so ADOP derives a\n// deterministic id server-side (Gate 6J-C1 IDEMPOTENCY LOCK — never an n8n\n// execution id or receive-time, which would break on a genuine retry).\n//\n// text is Fonnte's BUTTON TEXT field, never a plain-message fallback —\n// only body.message is the canonical message field.\nconst input = $input.item.json;\nconst body = input && input.body && typeof input.body === 'object' ? input.body : input;\n\nconst inboxId = Number(body.inboxid);\nconst providerMessageId = Number.isInteger(inboxId) && inboxId > 0 ? `fonnte:inbox:${inboxId}` : undefined;\n\nconst envelope = {\n  provider: 'fonnte',\n  channel: 'whatsapp',\n  senderAddress: String(body.sender || body.from || ''),\n  receiverAddress: String(body.device || ''),\n  messageText: String(body.message || ''),\n  providerTimestamp: String(body.timestamp || ''),\n};\nif (providerMessageId) {\n  envelope.providerMessageId = providerMessageId;\n}\n\nreturn [{ json: { envelope, canonicalBody: JSON.stringify(envelope) } }];"
      },
